# Tesla P100 (sm_60). Every op resolves to kernels/qwen/qwen3_5/nvidia/ (the
# card .so only exports NVLink helpers).
#
# Measured by @apollo-mg on a 2x Tesla P100-PCIE-16GB box (PHB, no NVLink),
# driver 580.178.04, CUDA 12.4, SM clock locked at 1328 MHz, 2-stage pipeline.
# unsloth Qwen3.8-27B Q6_K (~20.9 GiB), 64 trunk layers + 1 NextN. These are
# spite-bench output, not generated on the 6x P100 target.
#
# Reference on the same box and file: llama.cpp (-sm layer) decodes at 8.90
# tok/s and processes a 512-token prompt at 117.5 tok/s.
#
# STILL MISSING for the AGENTS.md gate: the "before" row, which must be the
# generic fallback (kernels/generic/generic) on this same box:
#   cargo run --release -p spite-bench -- --model <Q6_K>.gguf --device cpu \
#     --n-prompt 16 --n-tokens 8 --n-runs 1
# NOTE: rows carrying a head sha were measured on that head. f85a2a2 is the
# first head where a 2-stage split takes the batched prefill path at all
# (7.89 vs 7.24 tok/s, 1.09x); the prefill column is still the number to beat.
#
# Later heads change the numbers and are NOT reflected in the rows above, so
# re-run before quoting them:
#   - the MTP prompt prefill is now batched (was one NextN pass per prompt
#     token, the -6.6% between f85a2a2's 7.89 and caa2d72's 7.37);
#   - the speculative verify is now one batched trunk pass over [tok, d0..dK-1]
#     with a GDN state rollback, so `--mtp` should finally beat plain decode;
#   - `kBatchChunk` 4 -> 8 (1.22x on the FFN-gate shape, measured on an RTX 5090
#     through PTX JIT, not on these P100s);
#   - the batched GEMV now tiles output rows (`kRowTile` 4) and reuses the
#     activation across them, which is the measured 75% of that kernel: 1.42-1.52x
#     on the prefill projections, 1.08-1.26x at the verify width, again measured
#     on the RTX 5090 through PTX JIT. Every row below predates it.
# `spite-bench --mtp` now also prints `draft-vs-trunk TV`, the draft/trunk
# distribution divergence, so a 100% acceptance column can be told apart from a
# head that merely copies the trunk.
Qwen3.8-27B-Q6_K.gguf (unsloth) [cuda (sm_60), 2x P100-PCIE, 2-stage]               6.7 tok/s  prefill   6.9 tok/s  TTFT  1020.7 ms  mem 20969 MiB  (n=5)
Qwen3.8-27B-Q6_K.gguf (unsloth) [cuda (sm_60), 2x P100-PCIE, 2-stage, n_prompt=512, f1cc494] 6.7 tok/s  prefill   7.2 tok/s  TTFT 70771.5 ms  mem 20969 MiB  (n=3)
Qwen3.8-27B-Q6_K.gguf (unsloth) [cuda (sm_60), 2x P100-PCIE, 2-stage, n_prompt=512, f85a2a2] 6.7 tok/s  prefill   7.9 tok/s  TTFT 64900.0 ms  mem 20969 MiB  (n=3)
